{"id": "86252", "name": "פרבולה – קודקוד, מוקד ומדריך ממשוואה נתונה (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>The equation given below represents a parabola:</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:0}}. \\]</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Find the coordinates of the vertex, \\((x_c,y_c)\\), the coordinates of the focus, \\((x_f,y_f)\\) and the equation of the directrix.</p><p>Give your answer as a list containing (in this order) the coordinates of the vertex, the coordinates of the focus and the equation of the directrix.</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\( [ x_c, y_c, x_f, y_f, eq ] \\) = [[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:12px\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Outline:</b> Bring the equation to one of the two standard forms of a parabola with vertex \\((x_c,y_c)\\); the vertex, the focus and the directrix are then read off.</div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 1 — The standard forms</b><br><p>If the equation can be written in the form</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ (y - y_c) = a\\cdot(x-x_c)^2, \\]</p><p>then the vertex is given by \\((x_c,y_c)\\), the focus is given by \\((x_c, y_c +\\frac{1}{4a})\\), and the directrix by \\(y = y_c - \\frac{1}{4a}\\).</p><p>Or, if it can be written in the form</p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ (x - x_c) = a\\cdot(y-y_c)^2, \\]</p><p>then the vertex is given by \\((x_c,y_c)\\), the focus is given by \\((x_c + \\frac{1}{4a}, y_c)\\), and the directrix by \\(x = x_c - \\frac{1}{4a}\\).</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Step 2 — The given equation</b><br>The equation \\({{CT:0}}\\)    can be written as:<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:1}}{{CT:2}} = ({{CT:3}}) . \\]</p>Giving, \\(a = {{CT:1}}\\), the coordinates of the vertex are  \\(({{CT:4}},{{CT:5}})\\), the coordinates of the focus are \\(({{CT:6}},{{CT:7}})\\) and the directrix is \\({{CT:8}}\\).</div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "correctanswer", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "Result-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "Result-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"